<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea April agricultural import prices up-AFTAK.</title>
<headline>S.Korea April agricultural import prices up-AFTAK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's agricultural commodities import prices rose in April from the previous month on gains in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>AFTAK, established in 1970, currently has 13,200 members representing more than 45,000 overseas suppliers.</p>
<p>Its member firms handle over 82 percent of the country's total imports.</p>
<p>April import prices for agricultural commodities were as follows:  </p>
<p>(price in US$ per tonne on C&amp;F)</p>
<p> COMMODITY   TYPE			 ORIGIN     Apr    Mar</p>
<p> Wheat	 Soft White		 U.S.	 201    188</p>
<p> Wheat	 Hard Red Winter	  U.S.	 219    212</p>
<p> Wheat	 Dark Northern Spring   U.S.	 221    219</p>
<p> Corn	  No.3 yellow		U.S.	 145    154</p>
<p> Soybean     No.2			 U.S.	 350    340</p>
<p> Soymeal				    U.S.	 330    330</p>
<p> Tallow	TW (FOB)		   U.S.	 440    480</p>
<p> Palm oil    Olein (FOB)		Malaysia   590    575</p>
<p> Sugar	 96-97pct		   Thailand   305    303</p>
<p> Coffee	NY No.2 (FOB)	    Brazil   4,220  4,141</p>
<p> Rubber	RSS No.3		   Malaysia 1,125  1,236</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
